  Well said.

  Here's a suggestion: use Explore mode.  If you start the game with
"nethack -X" it will use your saved game file to start up an explore
mode game.  Your save file will remain untouched.  

  This will leave you free to try off the wall techniques.  Or just try
the run and see where it gets you.  Take every (useless) identified
charged wand and see what happens when you break it in a crowd.
Breaking a wand of sleep might be especially useful.

  Two points:  1) If you Save out of the explore mode game it will
overwrite your save file.  Don't do that.  Quit out instead.  2) If you
Quit out of your real game it's gone for good.

  If you don't use this to identify items this probably isn't cheating.
Thinking about it past that can bring on a headache.  Think of it as a
shortcut to using Wizard mode to set up a really good duplicate of your
current game.

  What it's really good for is seeing how you'll do on the Ascension Run
and in the Endgame.


